{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773077048,"nonce":"zu97bxfAY9kZvt3Vz69fK5Sk/NU=","title":"Service worker NetworkFirst strategy defeats Cache-Control: no-store on graph API","message":"vite.config.ts configures Workbox with a NetworkFirst handler for /api/* with a 1-hour expiration cache. Workbox intercepts fetches at the service worker level before the browser HTTP cache, so the Cache-Control: no-store headers added to FastAPI graph endpoints have no effect in the PWA context.\n\nFix: change the urlPattern for /api/graphs/* to use NetworkOnly handler (no caching). Keep the server-side Cache-Control header as defense-in-depth for non-PWA clients.\n\nRelevant config in vite.config.ts:\n  runtimeCaching: [{\n    urlPattern: /^https?:\\/\\/.*\\/api\\/.*/i,\n    handler: \"NetworkFirst\",\n    options: { cacheName: \"api-cache\", expiration: { maxAgeSeconds: 3600 } }\n  }]\n\nThis means the original staleness bug (PWA serving stale graph state on reload) is NOT fixed by the Cache-Control change alone.","files":null}]}